### API – documentation
### Flow: 1) start a job  2) check its status  3) get the images
### Local:  run Azurite + `dotnet run --project api`
### Azure:  comment out the local baseUrl and uncomment the Azure one

# @baseUrl = http://localhost:5078
@baseUrl = https://ssp1-api-np.kindground-b58735cf.germanywestcentral.azurecontainerapps.io

### 1. Start a new job
# Returns 202 Accepted with the jobId.
# The images are generated in the background (start-jobs queue -> process-image queue).
# @name startJob
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs

### The jobId from the response above is used in the requests below
@jobId = {{startJob.response.body.$.jobId}}

### 2. Status and progress of the job
# Returns status (Queued / Processing / Completed), totalImages, finishedImages and progressPercent.
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{jobId}}

### 3. Images of the job
# Returns a SAS link per finished image (read-only, valid for 1 hour).
# Can be called while the job is still running: returns the images finished so far.
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{jobId}}/images

### 4. Status of a job that does not exist
# Returns 404 Not Found.
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/rbdjsdi339383

### 5. Images of a job that does not exist
# Returns 404 Not Found.
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/djdn3763/images